WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.067
-It's always good to see you.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.200
Thank you for playing
any game with me

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.000
and doing bits. I love it.
-Come on, man.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.167
That was -- it's crazy fun.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:07.667
-I was almost going to see you
on the "SNL"

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:09.601
Christmas episode
with Paul Rudd.

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:12.267
-Yeah, that was an almost
catastrophe

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:14.000
that almost happened.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.534
-Here's you and whoever...
-It slammed into the wall.

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:19.000
-...at the end of --
at the end of the night.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.634
-That's just five people when it
should be 60, but...

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:23.934
-Tom Hanks, yeah.
And Che and...

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:26.000
-Yeah. Poor Paul Rudd, man.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.501
He'll get his gift back, though.

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:29.000
-Yeah, I mean, I felt bad
for him,

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.734
because I was gonna
come in for that.

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:32.667
That's when I tested positive.

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:34.000
-Oh, so your business
is out there?

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.334
So we can say that you...?
-Yeah, we can say, yeah.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.367
-Okay, cool.
-Yeah, I talk of it, yeah.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:39.033
-But that was dirty. You were
living dirty that morning.

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.734
-I wouldn't call it that.

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:44.067
But what was that week
like though?

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:45.901
Because that week you planned
to have a show, right?

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:49.601
-Yeah, we were working like it
was a regular week on the show,

00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:52.601
and you know, we -- Tom Hanks
was coming because it was going

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:54.601
to be Paul Rudd's fifth show,
you know?

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:56.567
-Yeah, five timers.
-Four and half.

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:59.934
But he still got his jacket.

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:01.334
-Yeah.
-But yeah, we were working

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.234
like a regular week,
and then numbers were just

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:06.534
going crazy in New York,
and by Saturday, you know,

00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:07.834
NBC people just called it.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.000
They were just like,
"Send everybody home."

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.734
We figured out a way to like,
you know, keep whoever.

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:15.868
I was asked to stay and a couple
other people, I guess

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:17.801
and a small crew, and then,
you know,

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.234
we put on whatever show we had.

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:21.601
Luckily, like they didn't call
it until Saturday,

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:23.400
so we were able to get
some like new stuff

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.634
that had been pretaped and
stuff that week or whatever.

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:27.767
But yeah, it was crazy.
It was not --

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:28.801
-Thanks for being there,

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:29.934
and thanks for putting
on the show.

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:31.434
-I had to represent
for the cast, baby.

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:32.767
-Come on, bud.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:34.901
Show must go on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:37.467
-The show must always go on.

00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:40.067
-Another great season of "SNL"
this year,

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:42.934
but one person that stuck
out that stole

00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:44.868
the show is Dionne Warwick
came on the show

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:46.067
and was so funny.

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:47.000
She was great.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.267
-Did y'all see Dionne Warwick?

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:50.367
-It was so good.
-She was incredible.

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:52.100
-She was incred-- She nailed it.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.033
But here's one thing,
she tweeted at you

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:56.701
before she was on the show
because somebody said

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:58.000
like hey, you should do "SNL"
this season.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.267
And she said, "That's a question
for the persons

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:02.400
who run the show,
Lorne or Kenan."

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.934
-Yeah. Okay, back story.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:08.300
Ego Nwodim has been doing an

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.033
incredible impression
of Dionne Warwick.

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:11.501
She does a Dionne Warwick show,

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:15.601
and I think it, you know,
kind of triggered her radar.

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:18.534
So I think Black people migrate
towards each other.

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:20.968
So for some reason she thinks
that I represent "SNL"

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:23.334
and she can speak through me,
you know,

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:25.367
to get her message across.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:26.801
Like, if we see a crowd
of people and we see

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:28.067
a Black person in the crowd,
we're going to go them

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:29.601
and ask them like, "Who made the
chicken?" I guess.

00:02:29.601 --> 00:02:31.534
I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:33.300
I don't know.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.000
-I just -- I gotta announce
today that

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.534
"SNL" is coming back next week.

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:38.567
-That's right.
We are back next week.

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:40.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.400
-Ariana DeBose.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.167
-Ariana DeBose, that's right.

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:44.334
-Roddy Ricch.

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:45.567
-Yeah, Roddy Ricch.
He's amazing.

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:46.567
-That's going to be a good show.

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:47.734
-You like that song
Roddy Ricch did?

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.334
-The last time
we saw each other,

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:51.000
I was just talking
to the audience,

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.434
but we were in D.C. for Lorne.

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:54.868
Lorne got
the Kennedy Center honor.

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:56.467
-Yeah, congratulations to him.

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:57.968
-Yeah, that was --
Dude, you killed that night.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.667
-Thank you.
-I forget what joke you told,

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:02.868
but you crushed.
-Okay, so my first opening joke,

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:04.400
I just thought was like,
you know,

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.634
just a cool opener or whatever.

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:08.701
But it was --
it killed everyone.

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:10.801
-Killed.
-So it was...

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:12.601
-Something.
-You know, you usually don't get

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:15.267
invited to Washington, D.C.
to talk about your boss,

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:17.067
especially in front
of the president

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:19.601
and especially under oath.

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:21.601
-Yeah.
-Right?

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:22.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.000
Just alright?

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.200
When you're in D.C.,
destroyed the room.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.634
-Yeah, I told you though
afterwards, they cut to Biden.

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:32.501
The president was there,
and he was clapping.

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:34.667
He was like laughing.
-Joe Biden clapped.

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:37.467
-Like, under the mask you can
tell he's laughing,

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:38.634
laughing, laughing.

00:03:38.634 --> 00:03:39.968
And I go, "Just crushed."

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:41.100
-That was crazy.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.334
A shout out to David.

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:44.133
He was producing that show,
and he wrote that.

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:45.601
He knows his audience.

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.534
-He knows his audience, man.
They knew it.

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:49.801
But I thought it was so --
-Straightforward,

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:51.300
strict law jokes.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:58.234
-I liked it, because, you know,
it's fun to have funny friends.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:03:59.467
-Yeah, it's the best.
-And funny people.

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:00.601
We did bits all the day long.

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:01.901
-It's the best.

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:04.167
Like, whenever we are able to --
because we don't get

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:06.234
to see the elders much,
you know what I'm saying?

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:08.801
Like, once you leave the show.
-Thank you.

00:04:08.801 --> 00:04:11.567
-You know, so it's nice
to get around.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:13.000
-I'm the elder now. Wow.
-You're one of the --

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.601
our elders. You know?

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:17.400
You're definitely my big brother
for sure.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.868
-Appreciate it.
-But ain't that sweet?

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:20.501
But it's true.

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:22.934
I was 25 when I came
to the show.

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:23.934
You know what I mean?
-Yeah.

00:04:23.934 --> 00:04:24.934
-It's when you first start.

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:27.200
But it's fun to be
around you guys,

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.767
also the new cast,
Steve Martin was there.

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.200
-That's what I'm saying.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.834
As soon as I walked in,
Kevin Nealon and Steve Martin

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:33.167
sitting there, like,
going over jokes.

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:34.734
-Kevin Nealon did
the funniest bit to me.

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:36.868
The whole day was all bits.
-Yeah.

00:04:36.868 --> 00:04:39.200
-Amy Poehler doing bits,
Kristen Wiig doing bits.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.901
The best.
-Exhausting, but it's the best.

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:43.200
-The whole day was bits.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.567
-Yeah, very passive aggressive
hazing.

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:47.601
-Everyone was doing bits,
and I got to the hotel.

00:04:47.601 --> 00:04:50.100
I go, I'll have a couple, like,
an hour of non-bits...

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.400
-Right.
-...just so I can --

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.300
-Just to relax and shut the
brain down from bits.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.667
-Yeah, shower off the bits.

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:57.601
-Yeah.
-But I get -- I get out --

00:04:57.601 --> 00:04:59.033
I get out of the car
and Jim Downey

00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:00.367
is standing in front
of the hotel.

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:01.801
Here comes one
of the best writers.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:04.133
-Here comes one of greatest
from the beginning.

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:05.133
-From the beginning?
-Yes.

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:06.300
-Of "Saturday Night Live."
-Yeah.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.100
-Haven't spoken to Jim
in probably three years.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:11.067
-Yeah.
-Just life happens.

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:12.467
But I go, "I have to do a bit."

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:14.534
-Immediately.
-I haven't seen the guy.

00:05:14.534 --> 00:05:16.334
He's one of the funniest dudes.
-No matter how tired you are,

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:17.701
there must be a bit
that's gotta happen.

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:20.267
-There has to be a bit so I came
out and I go --

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:23.367
it was the hotel and then they
had like two -- like a parking

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:26.868
garage and they had two poles
so that your car, you know?

00:05:26.868 --> 00:05:28.367
And I got out of the car
and I go,

00:05:28.367 --> 00:05:30.801
"Excuse me sir, is this to the
Washington monument?"

00:05:30.801 --> 00:05:33.267
-Classic.
-Because I'm in D.C.,

00:05:33.267 --> 00:05:34.634
and there's this tiny pole.

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.534
-Great.
-You know, in front of the...

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:37.934
And he --
without missing a beat --

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:40.767
he goes, "A lot of people assume
that that is, but it's not.

00:05:40.767 --> 00:05:42.567
It's actually --
it's actually this one."

00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:45.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:46.000
Did a bit.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.434
-Amazing.

00:05:47.434 --> 00:05:50.567
-That's the thing about the
environment of "SNL,"

00:05:50.567 --> 00:05:52.601
like you're around
such genius minds.

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:54.033
You haven't spoke to the
guy in three years.

00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:55.200
-Yeah.
-And you jump into

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.467
a bit like that.
-I want to talk about "Kenan"

00:05:57.467 --> 00:05:59.167
by the way, and I want to talk
about your Emmy

00:05:59.167 --> 00:06:00.200
nominations and all this stuff.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.501
-Me?
-Let's talk about "Kenan."

00:06:02.501 --> 00:06:03.701
More with Kenan Thompson
after the break.

00:06:03.701 --> 00:06:04.868
Stick around, everybody.

